From 5f1d292fed41b3758e0b1a1a479ac13945380e6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 22:47:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 130/135] feat: the AUTO meter no longer lets the sky own the
 exposure outdoors (Sky Weight)

Outdoors the sky is about half the frame at 0..+2 stops over the sunlit ground.
Centre-weighting is symmetric about a centred horizon, so it does not reduce the
sky's share at all, and the 50-90 % metering band was therefore entirely sky: the
camera exposed the SKY to mid grey and the ground landed 0.5-1.8 stops under it,
the shade 4-5 stops under - black. Indoors the sky through a door is under 20 %
and already outside the band, which is why indoors was fine.

The fix is a matrix meter's sky detection with the engine's classifier
(decisions/s8-metering-sky.md, approach A):

- SceneReferredMeterHistogramCS binds the quarter-res linear depth
  (m_pTexLinearDepthScaled[1], same grid as the source) as t1. Its .y is the 4x4
  minimum linear depth and the linearise pass preserves an exact 1.0 for the
  sky, so .y >= 1 means every pixel under the texel is sky; the mask weight of
  such a texel is multiplied by MeterHistParams.w before binning.
- New Cinematic Camera member 'mtsk' MeterSkyWeight / "Sky Weight", 0..1,
  default 0.25 (1 = previous behaviour, 0 = the sky is invisible to the meter
  and an all-sky frame holds). Published as Global_User_MeterSkyWeight beside
  MeterMode; the value the dispatch used comes back with the bins.
- The histogram target grows from 64x1 to 66x1: columns 64/65 accumulate the
  sky texel count and the sky weight that actually entered the bins. The
  readback latches the sky weight and source texel count at download time and
  publishes skyFraction / skyMeterShare / skyWeight on SSceneReferredMeterHistogram.
- r_HDRDebug 1 histogram line gains "sky NN% of frame x W = MM% of meter".
- README / ConsoleReference describe the parameter.

Off the switch nothing changes: the pass is not dispatched. The
r_SceneReferredMeterHistogram 0 log-mean fallback is untouched.

